# nr-office-pdf-ocr: OCR of PDF pages in mixdog-office-pdf (src/ocr/{mod,engine,install,tsv,layer}.rs)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The module is not part of the crate until the lines below are applied.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod limits;` (keep the list sorted: `analysis`, `contact_sheets`, `document`, `limits`, `ocr`, `render`, `search`):

    pub mod ocr;

After the last `pub use` line add:

    pub use ocr::{OcrContext, PageText, ocr_pdf, pdf_ocr_readiness, recognize_pdf_page_texts};

(The doc comment at the top of lib.rs may name `pdf-ocr.mjs`, `ocr-engine.mjs` and `ocr-engine-worker.mjs` among the ported files.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], keeping the list sorted, add (all workspace dependencies already in Cargo.lock; none is a new crate, only new edges of
mixdog-office-pdf: flate2 (gunzip of the language data and of a gzip engine asset), reqwest (the first-use downloads), sha2 (the
engine asset's pin), zip (a zip engine asset)):

    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    reqwest = { workspace = true }
    sha2 = { workspace = true }
    zip = { workspace = true }

and widen the existing tokio line (the engine registry uses `watch`, `Mutex`, `JoinSet` and `select!`):

    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "time", "process", "io-util", "sync", "macros"] }

[dev-dependencies], add (tests/ocr_engine.rs serves downloads from a local socket and builds archives; tests/twin_ocr.rs replays):

    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    sha2 = { workspace = true }
    zip = { workspace = true }

and replace the existing dev tokio line by:

    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "time", "net", "io-util", "sync", "macros"] }

`cargo update --workspace --offline` and `cargo hakari generate` only add these edges to the lock and to mixdog-workspace-hack's feature
unification if hakari wants it. `zip` is the workspace entry (`default-features = false, features = ["deflate"]`); the test writes a
stored archive, which needs no more.

