## Registration of pdf.ocr and the read tool's OCR path (not this task)

`pdf.ocr` is registered in the Rust ext-host worker (nr-office-worker-pdf-methods: methods/pdf_ocr.rs); it calls
`mixdog_office_pdf::recognize_pdf_page_texts(&OcrContext::new(lanes, registry, note, data_dir), path, &pages, languages, cancel)`.
`office.run` (nr-office-pdf-content-ops: `ocr_pages`) and the sessionless readiness action call `ocr_pdf` and `pdf_ocr_readiness`. This task adds no protocol
method, so SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs is unchanged by it.

## The engine pin (blocks real recognition; the owner decision 'OCR engine' names it)

`src/ocr/install.rs` `ENGINE_ASSETS` is empty on purpose: an entry (platform key `win32-x64`, `linux-x64`, `darwin-arm64`, the asset's
URL, the lowercase hex sha256 of the published file, `Gzip` or `Zip`, the program's path inside it) is added only with the real hash of
a published release asset of Tesseract 5.5.1 (Apache-2.0). Until it is, `ensure_engine` answers "OCR is not available on this platform
(<key>): no OCR engine is published for it" and `pdf_ocr_readiness` reports `available: false` on a machine that has not installed one.
